    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nCoder BootstrapWorker returns success after the archive upload acknowledgement rather than after extraction, installation, and AO worker launch succeed.\n\n## Root cause\n\nbootstrapThroughPTY returns after receiving __AO_UPLOAD_DONE__. It does not await the existing final __AO_BOOTSTRAP_OK__ or __AO_BOOTSTRAP_FAILED__ result. Closing at that point can also leave streamPTYOutput blocked on an unconsumed unbuffered channel.\n\n## Required fix\n\n- Keep the buffered PTY connection alive after upload completion.\n- Await explicit bootstrap success/failure or process/transport termination.\n- Propagate extraction, sudo/user creation, binary installation, and worker-launch failures to the reconciler.\n- Ensure all stream goroutines terminate on success, failure, cancellation, and disconnect.\n- Add tests for success, post-upload command failure, transport closure, and cancellation without goroutine leaks.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nBootstrapWorker returns nil only after __AO_BOOTSTRAP_OK__. A post-upload __AO_BOOTSTRAP_FAILED__ reaches reconciliation as an error. No output goroutine remains blocked when the method returns.\n\nThis is a merge blocker discovered in the independent review of #4624 and must be merged into the #4624 branch before that PR lands.",
